SOURCE-AVAILABLE LICENCE
========================

This software is source-available, not open source. The source is published so
that it can be read, inspected and used — not so that it can be taken.


1. What you may do

   a. View, read and study the source code.
   b. Run the software for your own personal use, including making résumés for
      yourself with it, for any purpose, including applying for paid work.
   c. Keep a private copy for your own use, and modify that private copy for
      your own use.
   d. Link to it, write about it, quote short extracts of the code when
      discussing or reviewing it.


2. What you may not do without the prior written permission of the copyright
   holder

   a. Redistribute this software, in whole or in substantial part, modified or
      unmodified, by any means, including publishing it in another repository
      or hosting it as a service.
   b. Publish derivative works, including re-skins, forks offered to others,
      ports to other languages or frameworks, and templates extracted from it.
   c. Sell it, or include it in anything sold, rented or offered as a paid
      service.
   d. Remove or obscure the copyright notices in the source, in the user
      interface, or in this file.


3. Your own content is yours

   This licence covers the software only. It does not apply to anything you
   write, upload or produce with it. Your résumé, your text, your photograph,
